venue Pub","shared_categories":"Mediterranean, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"_393npnr0Dw1aGKy83x_0A","review_id":"KYBcLUG5ihRoy1fPMYB6YQ","date":"2015-12-07T18:29:50","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9422647356987,"text_excerpt":"I've heard amazing things about Paladar 511, and finally got a chance to grab brunch with a friend at this beautiful location right past Elysian Fields on Marigny St. The location is beautiful. If I could live in it I would. Tall, communal tables with fresh flowers, large booths for big groups, what looks to be a private dining area upstairs, and comfortable upholstered chairs. Vampires beware, a ton of natural light, open kitchen, and beautiful chandeliers. Their brunch menu is simple, with ten items and a choice of some sides. Our waitress was extremely patient with us since my friend was struggling to choose between various dishes (a good thing, in my opinion). I enjoyed the Bloody Mar..."},{"business_id":"_393npnr0Dw1aGKy83x_0A","review_id":"JKgIc6a9aGU8pbgRFHiKBw","date":"2017-07-09T02:30:56","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9417923092842102,"text_excerpt":"Delicious! I damn near overdosed on traditional Cajun cuisine during my last trip to New Orleans. Not complaining, but variety is a good thing! I was really craving some pizza, so my bf and I - who doesn't eat pizza - comprised on Italian. Lots of really unique menu items and flavor pairings. I tried the lamb pizza which included some really delicious Tzatziki sauce --I don't even like that stuff!! The venue is very contemporary with an industrial,chic feel. Service was also great. They were behind on my pizza order, so they graciously comped my meal AND my second glass of wine. Thanks! It was pretty busy on a Friday night so reservations may be smart."},{"business_id":"_393npnr0Dw1aGKy83x_0A","review_id":"pc7VVBV238yRFf8XWCoGEA","date":"2018-12-04T01:48:09","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.939225971698761,"text_excerpt":"The ambiance of this place is amazing. It's tucked away toward the end of the street an if you're not looking for it you would absolutely miss it. It's definitely a hidden gem in the area. I started with the aviation cocktail while I waited at the bar. When I was seated I decided I wanted to try a little bit of everything. We ordered the little gem salad which I was skeptical about because I'm not a fan of mint but I love beets and I was intrigued. The mint wasn't over powering and it gave the right compliments. Next we ordered the curry carrots which was nothing like I imagined, it was so much better. I will say it's not what you would expect from a curry dish but you will enjoy it. The ..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"_393npnr0Dw1aGKy83x_0A","photo_id":"K2ddToAAhMY1WuOdxys0Qg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/K2ddToAAhMY1WuOdxys0Qg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8628169894218445},{"business_id":"_393npnr0Dw1aGKy83x_0A","photo_id":"bVN7ocBqRSgkbcRUZVZ7fw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/bVN7ocBqRSgkbcRUZVZ7fw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8486751317977905},{"business_id":"_393npnr0Dw1aGKy83x_0A","photo_id":